WEBVTT

00:48.770 --> 00:52.070
<i>That concludes the performance from the Sou Drums Group.</i>

00:52.070 --> 00:55.320
<i>Please enjoy the upcoming Bon dance.</i>

00:56.030 --> 00:57.530
Cheers!

01:01.540 --> 01:05.440
There's something I wanna try out at our next gig...

01:02.840 --> 01:05.440
Sorry guys, I've gotta head off.

01:05.440 --> 01:06.290
What's the rush?

01:06.290 --> 01:09.960
I have to be up early to get to Kitasenju tomorrow.

01:09.960 --> 01:12.820
Good luck, Mr. Civil Engineer!

01:14.260 --> 01:15.880
Thanks for coming!

01:17.620 --> 01:19.560
You seem a little down, Aki.

01:19.560 --> 01:21.560
Not at all.

01:21.560 --> 01:23.200
You got work tomorrow?

01:23.200 --> 01:24.520
Just the late shift.

01:24.520 --> 01:27.220
In that case, let's keep drinking!

01:27.220 --> 01:30.040
Excuse me! Can I get another draught beer?

01:38.340 --> 01:40.440
Oh, shut up...

01:46.230 --> 01:48.080
Yes, hello?

01:48.080 --> 01:50.560
Miyagawa? Long time.

01:50.560 --> 01:51.640
Who're you?

01:51.640 --> 01:55.090
I guess you might've forgotten me... It's me, Yoshioka.

01:55.090 --> 01:57.510
Yoshioka-sensei?!

01:58.640 --> 01:59.880
<i>You been keeping well?</i>

01:59.880 --> 02:01.560
Y-Yes...<i></i>

02:01.560 --> 02:04.180
<i>I heard you've been doing a great job as a pro in Tokyo.</i>

02:04.180 --> 02:06.430
W-Well, I suppose...<i></i>

02:06.430 --> 02:10.580
<i>Thing is, there's something I wanna talk to you about.</i>

02:10.580 --> 02:13.270
<i>We're reviving Kariyama's Autumn Drum Festival.</i>

02:14.640 --> 02:19.000
<i>A whole bunch of us are getting together. What's it been, 15 years now?</i>

02:19.000 --> 02:23.760
<i>But, well, we don't really have anyone to do the coaching</i>

02:23.760 --> 02:27.920
<i>and I've gotten a little rusty myself. What do you say, Miyagawa?</i>

02:27.920 --> 02:32.250
<i>Do you reckon you could come back for a little while and teach these guys?</i>

02:33.480 --> 02:37.500
<i>Even I knew that I was pathetic.</i>

02:38.360 --> 02:43.760
<i>I may call myself a professional, but I'm still keeping a second job to make ends meet.</i>

02:43.760 --> 02:45.900
<i>I had no plans or goals for the future.</i>

02:46.860 --> 02:51.230
<i>Someone like me shouldn't be qualified to teach others.</i>

03:05.490 --> 03:07.900
You haven't changed a bit, Miyagawa.

03:07.900 --> 03:09.660
Neither have you, Yoshioka-sensei.

03:09.660 --> 03:11.860
The car's this way.

03:11.860 --> 03:14.000
Oh, I'll take this for you.

03:15.260 --> 03:17.460
<i>That's right...</i>

03:18.060 --> 03:22.930
<i>There's no way that we're still... the same as we were back then.</i>

03:27.380 --> 03:29.640
Kumamoto sure has changed.

03:29.640 --> 03:31.850
The city's expanded all the way out to here.

03:31.850 --> 03:35.560
All else aside, it <i>is</i> an ordinance-designated city.

03:35.560 --> 03:38.980
Even our town combined with the neighbouring ones and became Mitomi Town.

03:38.980 --> 03:41.520
I don't think I'll ever get used to that name.

03:41.520 --> 03:44.570
Kariyama will always be Kariyama. Right, Sensei?

03:44.570 --> 03:46.560
Oh, don't say that.

03:46.560 --> 03:50.060
Thanks to that, we've got a lot more people taking part in the festivals now.

03:50.060 --> 03:51.580
But you know, I'm relieved.

03:51.580 --> 03:54.700
You're finally showing your Kumamoto dialect.

03:54.700 --> 03:56.840
I was worried you'd changed.

04:12.660 --> 04:14.400
I'll stop by to pick you up tomorrow.

04:14.880 --> 04:16.680
Thank you very much.

04:25.120 --> 04:26.780
I'm home!

04:29.900 --> 04:30.870
Welcome home.

04:33.500 --> 04:34.920
Welcome home, Aki.

04:34.920 --> 04:37.630
I didn't know you'd be coming back too, Fumiko-nee-chan!

04:37.630 --> 04:40.860
I heard you were coming back,
so I thought I may as well show up too.

04:40.860 --> 04:42.840
Come on, Haruna. Say hello.

04:44.760 --> 04:48.160
You were so tiny the last time I saw you.

04:48.160 --> 04:50.280
I guess you don't remember me.

04:50.280 --> 04:52.390
Here you go. Share it around with everyone.

04:53.120 --> 04:55.940
My, isn't that nice, Haruna-chan?

04:55.940 --> 04:56.960
Yup!

04:56.960 --> 04:58.360
Say thank you, now.

04:58.360 --> 05:00.900
Thank you, onee-chan!

05:00.900 --> 05:03.360
If you're looking for Dad, he's out in the yard.

05:12.080 --> 05:13.860
I'm back, Grandma.

05:13.860 --> 05:17.500
Welcome home, Aki. We were all waiting to see you.

05:20.740 --> 05:22.960
Dad... I'm back.

05:23.960 --> 05:25.260
I see.

05:28.900 --> 05:33.420
You're probably tired from your trip.
Wanna go visit the onsen before dinner, Aki?

05:33.420 --> 05:35.350
You too, Haruna.

05:38.310 --> 05:42.270
I wanna stay with Granpa!

05:42.270 --> 05:48.240
<i>My father and I barely ever spoke to each other since I moved to Tokyo.</i>

05:51.990 --> 05:55.480
Ah, this feels great!

05:55.480 --> 05:59.260
I wonder how many years it's been since I had a bath with family.

05:59.260 --> 06:02.710
But it's a good thing Dad's taking care of Haruna while we're here.

06:02.710 --> 06:04.980
How's your husband doing?

06:04.980 --> 06:06.600
Same as ever.

06:06.600 --> 06:10.220
Always busy with work, and barely ever has time for us.

06:10.220 --> 06:13.010
And Dad's still his old self too.

06:13.010 --> 06:16.300
We haven't seen each other in so long,
yet he still acts like that.

06:16.300 --> 06:21.860
Well, it can't be helped. I'm the one who left to pursue Drumming as a profession after all.

06:21.860 --> 06:27.020
But hey, you're doing well in Tokyo as a professional, aren't you?

06:33.540 --> 06:38.520
<i>I told my sister to head back home first, and stayed behind to wander around old Kariyama Town.</i>

06:40.000 --> 06:44.140
<i>My old hometown, now called Mitomi Town.</i>

06:46.940 --> 06:49.300
I wonder why I came back.

06:58.780 --> 07:00.980
It's a cute song, isn't it?

07:01.700 --> 07:04.310
What is it, Aki?

07:05.320 --> 07:05.900
Drums...

07:05.900 --> 07:09.020
Oh, they're probably just practicing for the festival.

07:09.020 --> 07:11.540
It's the week after next, isn't it?

07:11.540 --> 07:13.160
I can't wait!

07:13.160 --> 07:14.860
Wait, Aki?

07:31.430 --> 07:36.680
<i>I can't describe it very well, but that sound was special.</i>

07:36.680 --> 07:41.100
<i>"This is drumming!" I thought.</i>

07:48.440 --> 07:50.400
Hey, Aki!

07:50.400 --> 07:52.320
They were so cool!

07:52.320 --> 07:55.570
I don't really get it, but whatever, they were so cool!

07:55.570 --> 08:00.120
Mum! I'm gonna play in the Drums Festival!

08:02.330 --> 08:03.180
Hello.

08:03.180 --> 08:03.980
Hello.

08:03.980 --> 08:05.290
Heya.

08:05.290 --> 08:06.840
Hello!

08:08.590 --> 08:10.660
You're the new kid, right?

08:10.660 --> 08:12.050
Umm...

08:12.050 --> 08:13.840
Miyagawa Aki!

08:13.840 --> 08:16.300
I'm Yoshioka. Nice to meet you, Aki-chan.

08:16.300 --> 08:19.430
Nice to meet you, Yoshioka-sensei!

08:19.430 --> 08:22.900
Come on, now, I'm still a university student.

08:22.900 --> 08:24.980
Don't go calling me Sensei.

08:26.640 --> 08:28.760
She called you 'Sensei'!

08:28.760 --> 08:30.570
Oi, Naoto!

08:40.620 --> 08:45.420
Ready, everyone? Now, slowly lift up your rutes.

08:55.300 --> 09:00.560
You've got pretty good form. If I didn't know otherwise, I'd think you were already experienced.

09:00.560 --> 09:03.880
But you're gripping your rutes a little too tightly, though.

09:03.880 --> 09:05.940
Got it, Yoshioka-sensei!

09:05.940 --> 09:08.150
Like I said, don't call me Sensei.

09:10.900 --> 09:12.860
Get it right!

09:20.820 --> 09:23.910
<i>I was captivated by the drums.</i>

09:33.420 --> 09:34.210
Begin!

09:43.560 --> 09:44.100
Next!

09:46.560 --> 09:51.000
<i>Beating the drums with everyone was really fun.</i>

09:51.000 --> 09:55.560
<i>But above all, it was that feeling
of being engulfed in the sound.</i>

09:51.760 --> 09:52.880
Next!

10:19.760 --> 10:22.350
Will the festival be okay to go ahead?

10:22.350 --> 10:26.320
They said the typhoon will pass by before tomorrow, so it should be fine.

10:26.320 --> 10:28.960
It's getting a bit dangerous. Let's head back inside.

10:44.990 --> 10:47.480
I was really worried for a bit there.

10:47.480 --> 10:49.080
I'm sure glad the typhoon's gone.

10:51.180 --> 10:52.680
Hey, Aki.

10:52.680 --> 10:53.960
What is it?

10:54.780 --> 10:56.580
Nevermind. It's nothing.

10:57.920 --> 11:03.040
<i>Thank you all for waiting. We will now begin the Drums Festival and ensuing tournament.</i>

11:03.040 --> 11:06.810
<i>The group from Yamaguchi will be starting off.</i>

11:13.020 --> 11:14.100
Look out!

11:15.230 --> 11:17.100
This is bad!

11:21.220 --> 11:23.920
<i>The festival was put on hold,</i>

11:23.920 --> 11:27.290
<i>and our first stage performance ended as a dream.</i>

11:28.600 --> 11:32.420
<i>It was decided that the Drums Festival would not take place the following year.</i>

11:32.420 --> 11:36.630
<i>Or the next year, or the year after that.</i>

11:37.340 --> 11:40.900
<i>It was as though the festival, and even the drums themselves,</i>

11:40.900 --> 11:44.740
<i>was forgotten by the town.</i>

11:44.740 --> 11:47.140
We're already 13 years old.

11:49.460 --> 11:51.660
You're the only one who's still a kid, Aki.

11:51.660 --> 11:53.730
Cute as a button, isn't she?

11:55.690 --> 11:58.150
"Kariyama Shrine"

11:58.150 --> 12:00.720
Hm? What's wrong, Aki?

12:00.720 --> 12:03.120
Uh... It's nothing.

12:06.580 --> 12:09.370
"Kariyama Middle School Graduation Ceremony"

12:07.760 --> 12:14.250
In the end, I never even ended up touching a set of drums all throughout middle shcool.

12:15.020 --> 12:16.100
Miyagawa.

12:16.920 --> 12:20.600
I heard you got in to Minami High. Good luck!

12:20.600 --> 12:23.480
W-Woah, I'm impressed!

12:23.480 --> 12:26.930
Who was it? Who'd you give it to?

12:29.060 --> 12:30.390
What is it?

12:30.390 --> 12:32.220
Nevermind. It's nothing.

12:50.660 --> 12:52.540
"Staff Room"

12:50.660 --> 12:55.750
I was really surprised to see that you became a school teacher!

12:55.750 --> 12:59.670
I was surprised too! Suddenly seeing a familiar face like that.

12:59.670 --> 13:04.010
But now I can call you "Yoshioka-sensei" for real!

13:05.380 --> 13:07.600
Have you already joined a club?

13:07.600 --> 13:10.350
Knowing you, you've probably joined the Drums Club, right?

13:10.350 --> 13:16.540
The Drums Club? It wasn't an option on our orientation leaflet.

13:16.540 --> 13:17.940
That's strange...

13:20.610 --> 13:26.000
Wow, you're right. It's been registered as a club, but it's currently inactive.

13:26.000 --> 13:30.620
But I suppose even drumming itself was discarded by everyone after that festival.

13:31.320 --> 13:35.540
Sensei... I still want to play the drums!

13:36.040 --> 13:36.920
Miyagawa...

13:36.920 --> 13:39.920
Please become the supervisor for the Drums Club!

13:39.920 --> 13:43.670
H-Hey, now, that's not really for me to decide.

13:43.670 --> 13:46.280
I'll do something about gathering the members.

13:46.280 --> 13:48.260
So please!

13:48.260 --> 13:51.500
I don't see a problem with it, Yoshioka-sensei.

13:51.500 --> 13:54.060
All of the drums are just gathering dust anyway.

13:54.620 --> 13:58.020
I'll make some new orientation leaflets.

13:59.920 --> 14:01.730
Thank you very much!

14:01.730 --> 14:11.070
New Students' Orientation

14:05.740 --> 14:09.100
<i>Next up is the Drums Club's demonstration.</i>

14:47.960 --> 14:50.200
<i>Did you see last night's show?</i>

14:51.960 --> 14:52.950
It's still not enough.

14:52.950 --> 14:55.870
Just leave it to me!

14:55.870 --> 14:59.710
Huh? Why should I have to play the drums?

14:59.710 --> 15:01.040
Megumi...

15:01.040 --> 15:04.840
More importantly, look at these nails!

15:04.840 --> 15:05.630
Aren't they cute?

15:05.630 --> 15:07.400
Take them off, and listen!

15:07.400 --> 15:11.590
Starting today, you're a member of the Drums Club!

15:14.350 --> 15:16.260
Drums?

15:16.260 --> 15:18.060
Akane...

15:18.060 --> 15:21.460
More importantly, have a look at this necklace.

15:21.460 --> 15:22.520
It's a skull.

15:22.520 --> 15:23.980
Take it off, and listen!

15:23.980 --> 15:28.100
Starting today, you're a member of the Drums Club!

15:32.680 --> 15:33.660
All right!

15:33.660 --> 15:34.840
Begin!

15:43.750 --> 15:48.080
<i>That feeling that I'd forgotten
began to stir in me once again.</i>

15:49.170 --> 15:53.680
<i>It was as though my heartbeat was synchronised with the beating of the drums.</i>

16:19.880 --> 16:25.460
<i>That's right. Long ago, this town resonated with the sound of drums.</i>

16:26.540 --> 16:28.460
<i>I want to bring back that sound.</i>

16:28.460 --> 16:31.680
<i>I want to revive the Autumn Drums Festival...</i>

16:34.920 --> 16:36.340
<i>...through the Drums Club!</i>

16:38.810 --> 16:43.020
"Kari High Festival"

17:43.750 --> 17:46.440
<i>The sound of drums, which had not been heard in a long time,</i>

17:46.440 --> 17:49.710
<i>was met with huge applause by those who watched on.</i>

17:49.710 --> 17:52.670
<i>It was a lively performance, fitting of these high schoolers.</i>

17:52.670 --> 17:57.590
They interviewed me after that. Look!

17:57.590 --> 18:02.160
The Kariyama Town Drums Festival has been on hold for 4 years,

18:02.160 --> 18:04.080
and we want to bring it back!

18:04.080 --> 18:05.980
We'll continue to do our best!

18:06.580 --> 18:07.420
See?

18:07.420 --> 18:09.800
Well, that's quite something.

18:09.800 --> 18:12.740
Oh! I saw myself in there!

18:12.740 --> 18:15.260
What do you think? What do you think?

18:15.260 --> 18:15.990
Hmm?

18:15.990 --> 18:19.240
You lot sure are trying very hard. Right, Dad?

18:19.820 --> 18:21.520
That kind of crap

18:21.520 --> 18:24.290
will never benefit you or anyone.

18:27.370 --> 18:29.290
Aki!

18:42.700 --> 18:49.620
<i>In all of my 3 years of high school, my father never once came to watch us play in the Cultural Festivals.</i>

18:53.260 --> 18:55.620
<i>And the Drums Festival was not revived.</i>

18:58.580 --> 19:02.880
After graduating from high school, I moved to Tokyo in order to

19:02.880 --> 19:04.950
become a professional drummer.

19:04.950 --> 19:06.160
Stay well.

19:06.160 --> 19:09.910
<i>My father wasn't there to see me off at that time either. </i>

19:10.840 --> 19:16.080
<i>An express train will be arriving at the station shortly.</i>

19:17.300 --> 19:19.360
<i>"I'll grab hold of my dreams,</i>

19:19.360 --> 19:21.300
<i>no matter what anyone else may think!"</i>

19:22.260 --> 19:24.560
<i>That's what I decided.</i>

19:33.810 --> 19:35.920
Did you sleep well?

19:35.920 --> 19:38.000
Yes, very soundly.

19:38.000 --> 19:40.840
Must've been nice to see your family after so long.

19:40.840 --> 19:41.910
It sure was.

19:44.980 --> 19:47.120
Wasn't it at the Community Hall?

19:47.120 --> 19:51.410
We've had a lot more people join,
so we had to shift to a new building.

20:17.520 --> 20:21.160
Umm, I was under the impression that it would be full of kids...

20:21.160 --> 20:24.100
I don't recall mentioning anything like that.

20:24.100 --> 20:25.490
Are you Miyagawa-senpai?

20:27.020 --> 20:32.220
Thank you for coming here all the way from Tokyo.

20:32.220 --> 20:35.980
I'm Sudou Misono, a 2nd year, in the Kariyama High Drums Club.

20:35.980 --> 20:38.090
I'm Yamakawa Yuzuki, 1st year.

20:38.090 --> 20:42.400
There's something I wanted to let you know about.

20:42.400 --> 20:46.300
It was actually our club who brought up the topic of reviving the Drums Festival.

20:46.300 --> 20:48.010
You guys did?

20:48.010 --> 20:51.520
That's right. As our last memories of this school.

20:53.220 --> 20:55.880
Kariyama High is being closed down.

20:55.880 --> 20:59.100
We'll be merging with Mitomi High at the end of the school year.

20:59.100 --> 21:02.570
The name "Kariyama" will disappear from the school, and from the town.

21:03.300 --> 21:07.480
But we were all born in Kariyama. We're all Kariyama people!

21:07.480 --> 21:08.940
As testament to that...

21:08.940 --> 21:14.290
As testament to that, we wanted to revive
Kariyama Shrine's Autumn Drums Festival.

21:14.290 --> 21:16.750
That's when we heard

21:16.750 --> 21:19.520
that a past student had once tried to do the same thing.

21:19.520 --> 21:23.720
That it was that same student who created our club in order to revive the festival.

21:23.720 --> 21:26.400
That there was a student who tried so hard to make it happen!

21:28.540 --> 21:30.600
Miyagawa-senpai.

21:30.600 --> 21:33.300
Please take part in the festival with us.

21:33.300 --> 21:35.690
Let's beat our drums together!

21:35.690 --> 21:37.520
Please!

21:39.360 --> 21:41.120
Together?

21:41.820 --> 21:45.070
You're not thinking of turning them down, are you?

21:45.070 --> 21:49.380
Don't worry, we taught these kids as much as we could.

21:49.380 --> 21:50.530
Just the basics, though!

21:50.530 --> 21:53.100
Megumi! Akane!

21:53.100 --> 21:55.900
<i>I'm</i> the one who did most of the teaching.

21:56.790 --> 21:59.460
Naoto! You too?

21:59.460 --> 22:01.680
What do you mean "too"?

22:01.680 --> 22:03.420
But hey, it's good to see you.

22:24.320 --> 22:26.080
Alright! Let's do this!

22:40.080 --> 22:43.220
<i>I believe that I'm happy.</i>

22:46.900 --> 22:48.940
<i>Happy that I came face-to-face with my dreams.</i>

22:49.820 --> 22:53.920
<i>And happy that, even now, I'm continuing towards those dreams.</i>

22:54.640 --> 22:59.440
<i>A small portion of my dreams have become a reality,</i>

22:59.440 --> 23:01.650
<i>though it's not just happiness that I feel.</i>

23:03.840 --> 23:07.060
<i>But I was afraid to let it go,</i>

23:08.000 --> 23:10.800
<i>and I found myself unable to turn back.</i>

23:13.940 --> 23:15.200
<i>But even so...</i>

23:19.940 --> 23:22.760
<i>But even so, when I look ahead...</i>

23:22.760 --> 23:24.090
<i>...my path is...!</i>
